  "name": "debug-tour",
  "$comment": "A guided tour of the debugger. A 1 kg cart on a spring (k = 10 N/m) and a damper (b = 2 N s/m), a bond-graph plant, is positioned by a sampled PID controller (library/CartPID.jl, Ts = 10 ms) whose drive force saturates at +-15 N. The reference steps from 0 to 1 m at t = 0.5 s. The controller has a planted bug: anti-windup is off (aw = 0), so the integrator winds up while the force is saturated, the cart overshoots past 1.2 m and an @events limit switch (library/LimitSwitch.jl) trips and cuts the drive. The docs walk through finding and fixing it with breakpoints, stepping, watches, a live parameter edit, Rewind and Replay.",
